@startuml architecture-beta-access-control-current
title Beta Access Control Current Architecture

' Purpose: Show the implemented app-level auth, beta gate, and restricted/admin policy boundaries.

actor "Browser User" as User
participant "Protected Pages and API Routes" as AppRoutes
participant "Page/API Guards" as AccessGuard
participant "Auth.js Email Auth" as AuthJs
participant "Resend Email Provider" as Resend
participant "Beta Access Policy" as BetaPolicy
participant "Admin Access Policy" as AdminPolicy
collections "Server Env: BETA_ALLOWED_EMAILS" as BetaEnv
collections "Server Env: BETA_ADMIN_EMAILS" as AdminEnv
participant "Drizzle + Auth.js Adapter" as Persistence
database "Postgres" as Postgres
participant "Readiness Services" as ReadinessServices
participant "Denied UI / 401 / 403" as DeniedUi

User -> AppRoutes: Request protected page or API
AppRoutes -> AccessGuard: Require beta access

alt No valid session
  AccessGuard -> AuthJs: Start email magic-link sign-in
  AuthJs -> Resend: Send login email
  User -> AuthJs: Open callback link
  AuthJs -> Persistence: Store or read user, session, and verification token
  Persistence -> Postgres: Auth.js tables
  AuthJs --> AccessGuard: Signed-in email identity
else Valid session exists
  AccessGuard -> AuthJs: Read signed-in identity
  AuthJs --> AccessGuard: Signed-in email identity
end

AccessGuard -> BetaPolicy: Check beta access
BetaPolicy -> BetaEnv: Load comma-separated allowlist
BetaPolicy -> BetaPolicy: Lowercase and trim emails

alt Invited beta identity
  BetaPolicy --> AccessGuard: Allow beta access
  AccessGuard --> AppRoutes: Continue protected request
  AppRoutes -> ReadinessServices: Run normal app behavior when requested
  ReadinessServices --> AppRoutes: Readiness payload
  AppRoutes --> User: Render beta app or API result
else Not invited or missing identity
  BetaPolicy --> AccessGuard: Deny beta access
  AccessGuard --> DeniedUi: Redirect or 401/403 response
end

User -> AppRoutes: Request restricted/admin API if one exists
AppRoutes -> AccessGuard: Require restricted access
AccessGuard -> AdminPolicy: Check admin access
AdminPolicy -> AdminEnv: Load comma-separated admin allowlist
AdminPolicy -> AdminPolicy: Lowercase and trim emails

alt Admin identity
  AdminPolicy --> AccessGuard: Allow restricted request
  AccessGuard --> AppRoutes: Continue restricted request
else Beta-only identity
  AdminPolicy --> AccessGuard: Deny restricted request
  AccessGuard --> DeniedUi: 403 response
end

note right of AccessGuard
Implemented boundary: protected pages and APIs call shared guards.
Auth routes, denied page, and framework internals stay outside
the protected beta request path.
end note

note right of AdminPolicy
Restricted/admin policy is implemented separately from beta access,
even though the repo does not yet expose a full admin UI.
end note

@enduml